### Teaching the repository

What a session had to work out, the next should be told, in the
repository's own CLAUDE.md: how to run its tests, where things live, a
convention you got wrong at first. A line or two each, in the same PR,
written as the repository's own documentation, never as notes from a
session. Tell the user what you added.

The architecture documentation says what is, and a change that moves a
part keeps it true in the same PR: `engineer` before it finishes,
`reviewer` as a finding when it was missed, and you yourself when you
work alone. Tell the user which documents changed.
